{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793531865478339001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nosophobic-zebraic-waterbug","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793529881944636001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e356854c-a6e7-4849-97d1-d15885c2b2a4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c670-c285-a0f9-4b40"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nA ticket-resolving `rebar` command run from a **clean worktree at `origin/main`** loads the\n**main checkout's** `rebar.toml`, not the worktree's own. Observed from\n`.rebar/worktrees/gate-cdac-6a3fecbb` (`HEAD=23fdf77f94c`, `behind=0`, `dirty=0`):\n\n```\n$ rebar show cdac-532f-0edb-422d\nWARNING rebar.config: rebar config (/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/rebar.toml): unknown key\n  'llm.overlap_drain' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)\n```\n\nThe named path is the main checkout, not the worktree.\n\n## Why it matters on this host\n\n`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` is **159 commits behind `origin/main`** and its `rebar.toml` is\n**locally modified** (`git diff --stat origin/main -- rebar.toml` = 24 insertions / 12\ndeletions). It still carries 3 occurrences of `overlap_drain`, one of the `[llm] overlap_*`\nkeys **removed** from `origin/main`'s `rebar.toml`. The worktree's own `rebar.toml` has 0.\n\nSo a config-driven code path — including gate paths that resolve a ticket — takes its\nsettings from a **stale, uncommitted file outside the tree under test**. `build_drift`\nalready warns about a stale *build*; nothing warns that the *config* came from elsewhere.\n\n## Measured scope\n\n| command (from the clean worktree) | loads main's rebar.toml? |\n|---|---|\n| `rebar show <ticket-id>` | yes (1 warning) |\n| `rebar list --status=open` | no |\n| `rebar explain plan` | no |\n\nSo it is the **ticket-resolution** path, not config discovery in general.\n\n## Evidence that discovery itself is correct\n\nIn-process, from the same worktree:\n\n```python\nfrom rebar._config_sources import _discover_project_config, repo_root\nrepo_root(None)            # -> .../worktrees/gate-cdac-6a3fecbb\n_discover_project_config() # -> (.../worktrees/gate-cdac-6a3fecbb/rebar.toml, 'toml')\n```\n\nBoth are correct. The escape therefore happens in whatever resolves config while opening\nthe **tracker** (`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`), whose parent directory is the\nmain checkout — a plausible mechanism is config being re-discovered from the tracker's\nparent rather than from the caller's repo root.\n\n## Suspected related symptom (same root)\n\nThe rebar **MCP server** reported `stale-store: the local ticket store is 19 commit(s)\nBEHIND the shared store` for `transition_ticket`, with a **byte-identical count across two\nattempts separated by a successful fetch**, while\n`rebar._store.freshness.store_freshness()` called directly returned\n`{\"fresh\": true, \"verdict\": \"fresh\", \"behind\": null}` from two different worktrees, and\n`git -C .tickets-tracker rev-list --count HEAD..origin/tickets` was `0`. The MCP server runs\nout of the same 159-commit-stale main checkout. Unproven that this is the same defect;\nrecorded here because both surfaces point at the main checkout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A ticket-resolving command run from a worktree loads **that worktree's** `rebar.toml`. Checked by: from a worktree whose `rebar.toml` differs from the main checkout's, `rebar show <id>` reports the worktree's path (or emits no foreign-config warning).\n- [ ] A regression test pins the behaviour: with a worktree config and a differing main-checkout config, the ticket-resolution path reads the worktree's.\n- [ ] The MCP `stale-store` divergence is either shown to share this root cause and fixed with it, or recorded as separate with its own evidence.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0df8-9ee6-24a6-4c39","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Ticket-resolution loads the main checkout's rebar.toml, not the worktree's","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c273434b-c04d-47d7-8c2e-7ab3a7137433","e356854c-a6e7-4849-97d1-d15885c2b2a4"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793531865478339001,"uuid":"8e59692b-ead3-4f9a-8073-07e58ccc6ab7"}